Changes:
--------

v1.2 - displays average cps-rate during ul/dl
v1.1 - supports hide and SkipIdlePorts
     - display of hide/mufflestatus
     - port 0-99 possible
     - whOlm is Pure -> can be loaded resident
     - little bugs in the installation-doc removed
v1.0 - first public release



Installation:
-------------

a) makedir pfiles:wholm

b) copy wholm, wholm.ansi to pfiles:wholm

c) edit your bbsmenu #30 computertypes, that they make sense with
   8 characters

d) rename the normal WHO command as you like (eg HULLAWHO)

e) create a command in bbsmenu

   WHolm #2pfiles:wholm/wholm <last port> <leveldisplay type> <olmusage>}|

   WHolm #2pfiles:wholm/wholm 3 nothing noolm}|
                                 text    olm
                                 graph

   last port        : eg. 3   : ports 0-3 are displayed
   leveldisplay type: nothing : no level is displayed
                      text    : the grouplevelname is displayed
                      graph   : the level is displayed as a bar/graph

   olmusage         : noolm   : no olm can be send. this must be used
                                during logon!
                      olm     : the user can send an olm to another port

f) if you want to load it resident:

   resident pfiles:wholm/wholm pfiles:wholm/wholm ADD


